values ('c9d0e1f2-3a4b-4c17-8d67-7e8f9a0b1c97', 'introduction-to-philosophy', 'Introduction to Philosophy', 'Introduction to Philosophy treats philosophy as disciplined questioning about reality, knowledge, value, meaning, and human life. Students learn to read, evaluate, reconstruct, and write arguments, then work through knowledge and skepticism, reality and metaphysics, mind and identity, free will, God and evil, moral theory and applied dilemmas, justice, science, language, and ancient, modern, and contemporary philosophy. The course ends by turning those questions into clear claims, charitable objections, rigorous replies, and polished prose.');

